# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.
.claude
input/
QualiBact assessment.csv
# Private notes / dev-only docs. Anything that should never leak to the
# public GitHub repo lives under /private/ or matches the named patterns
# below. Drop new internal docs in /private/ by default.
/private/
/CLAUDE.md
/TODO.md
/TODO-NABIL.md
/WORKPLAN.md
/WORKPLAN-v1.1.md
/OUTREACH-v1.1.md
/UI-CHANGES-*.md
/genomicx-frontend-styling-guide.md
/tests/fixtures/
# Survey-report output (PDF/MD/charts mailed back to respondents) lives
# under /private/. Belt-and-braces: also block content/feedback/ since
# scripts/survey_report.py previously wrote there.
/content/feedback/

# Static assets (hosted on Cloudflare R2) — but build-time data files that
# Next.js reads via fs.readFileSync must live in git so Cloudflare Pages
# can build. Bulk assets (PNGs, atb CSVs, refseq xz, assembly stats)
# stay R2-only. The exceptions below cover only what the build actually
# reads.
public/static/*
!public/static/species/
public/static/species/*
!public/static/species/*/
public/static/species/*/*
!public/static/species/*/*/
public/static/species/*/*/*
!public/static/species/*/*/manifest.json
!public/static/species/*/*/summary.csv
# /summary/ page reads these via fs.readFileSync at build time. Genus
# and priority-pathogens rollups are referenced via staticUrl() (R2),
# never fs-read, so they stay R2-only.
!public/static/summary/
public/static/summary/*.png

